.nh
.TH "TDDA EXAMPLES" 1 "January 2026" "3.0" "tdda examples manual"
.SH NAME
\fBtdda\fR examples \- Creates example data for TDDA

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtdda examples\fR
.br
\fBtdda examples\fR \fIMODULE\fP
.br
\fBtdda examples\fR \fIMODULE\fP \fIDIRECTORY\fP
.br
\fBtdda examples\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fP

.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
\fIMODULE\fP can be any of:
  - referencetest
  - constraints
  - rexpy
  - gentest
If not specified, all four will be used created.

.PP
\fIDIRECTORY\fP If specified, the example directories will be
            subdirectories of the specified directory
            (which should exist).

.SH DESCRIPTION
Write out example code and data for all examples, by default,
or for a particular module if specified.

.PP
If no module is specified, examples for all three are written out.

.PP
If no output directory is specified, the examples are
written to a subdirectory of the current directory.

.SH EXAMPLES
a. \fBtdda examples\fR
.br
   Creates all four example directories in \fB\&.\fR

.PP
b. \fBtdda examples gentest\fR
.br
   Creates examples-gentest in \fB\&.\fR

.PP
c. \fBtdda examples /tmp/tdda\fR
.br
   Creates all four as subdirectories of \fB/tmp/tdda\fR

.PP
d. \fBtdda examples rexpy t\fR
.br
   Creates examples-rexpy in subdirectory of \fB\&./t\fR
